From ea1a57250abc0d737653c73bf887d2755136882a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 04:56:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05634/11362] [outer-loop] add
 arc_log_analysis_plus_local_timing substrate, fix exp5215's false
 DURATION_TOO_SHORT

User asked to dig into the PHASE B1 flag -- exp5215 is the conductor's own
follow-through on my PAW-amortization research note from 2026-07-03, and it
landed a real, decisive result: paw_amortization_viable=False. Median
remaining actions (29.5) and p75 (43.75) both fall short of the estimated
break-even point (45.75 actions) for a mid-episode compile step to pay off
-- exactly the falsifiable gate the originating research note proposed,
executed correctly, giving an honest negative.

It got CRITICAL-flagged anyway: no substrate category recognized "read
several existing JSON logs plus one small, bounded, local (non-LLM) timing
measurement" -- a "torch_cuda:0" backend string in the timing evidence
pulled it toward the generic compute-bound-marker fallback, applying the
60s live_llm_inference floor to a task that never invokes an LLM at all.
duration_s=4.10s is genuinely plausible for the actual work done (reading
9 log files + one timing check correctly clamped to a 2.13s conservative
floor rather than trusted at its raw 1.3e-5s measurement).

This is the third time this exact bug class has appeared this session
(verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates/exp5161,
live_llm_embedding_extraction/exp5178, now this) -- each time a genuinely
new, legitimate substrate shape with no existing category to fit. Added
arc_log_analysis_plus_local_timing as the 7th legal inference_substrate
value (1.0s floor -- enough to rule out an implausibly-instant claim while
permissive for genuine log-analysis-plus-microbenchmark work), wired ahead
of the generic live_llm_inference check in duration_floor_for_artifact().
Also extended the METHODOLOGY_MISSING model_specs/target_model exemption
(previously only offline_arcade_live_agent_..._no_llm) to this substrate,
since it genuinely has no model to name either.

9 new tests (tests/python/test_adversarial_verify_log_analysis_local_timing_
substrate.py): recognition-function coverage, floor-priority-over-generic-
marker guard, an exact exp5215 reproduction now clean, a regression guard
confirming a fabricated near-instant claim (with a compute-bound marker
present, matching the real incident's shape) is still caught, and a
regression guard confirming the new substrate isn't a loophole for
artifacts that actually claim full generation. Full suite (263 tests)
green. Corpus-wide dry-run sanity check unchanged (5 previously-known
qualifying artifacts, no new flood).

Un-quarantined exp5215 itself: 0 CRITICAL flags now (was 1). One WARN
remains (missing random_seed/reproducibility_checksum) -- genuinely absent
from this conductor-authored artifact, left as an honest, non-blocking gap
rather than backfilled by the outer-loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
